    "question": {
      ":question/id": "26acd9d9-1047-5574-868b-18df16690056",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(- y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,1]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =- y\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 x\\,\\mathbf{j}+2 z\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(- \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =- t^{2}\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 t\\,\\mathbf{j}+2 t^{3}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 t\\,\\mathbf{j}+3 t^{2}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(- t^{2}\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t^{3}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- t^{2}\\right)+\\left(4 t^{2}\\right)+\\left(6 t^{5}\\right) \\\\ & =t^{2} \\left(6 t^{3} + 3\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(t^{2} \\left(6 t^{3} + 3\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[t^{6} + t^{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(1\\right)^{6} + \\left(1\\right)^{3}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(\\left(0\\right)^{6} + \\left(0\\right)^{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
