    "question": {
      ":question/id": "015a0892-0bd5-5009-af8c-07ee66ddf321",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left(2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(2 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t\\in [0,1]$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\qquad y=t^{2},\\qquad z=t^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =2 x\\,\\mathbf{i}+y\\,\\mathbf{j}+2 z\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\left(2 \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =2 t\\,\\mathbf{i}+t^{2}\\,\\mathbf{j}+2 t^{3}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(t^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ & =\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 t\\,\\mathbf{j}+3 t^{2}\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\left(2 t\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(2 t^{3}\\right)\\left(3 t^{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(2 t\\right)+\\left(2 t^{3}\\right)+\\left(6 t^{5}\\right) \\\\ & =2 t \\left(3 t^{4} + t^{2} + 1\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r} & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t \\left(3 t^{4} + t^{2} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ & =\\left[t^{6} + \\frac{t^{4}}{2} + t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(1\\right)^{6} + \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{4}}{2} + \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-\\left(\\left(0\\right)^{6} + \\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{4}}{2} + \\left(0\\right)^{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
